{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
  "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For decades, the Second Circuit has applied an invalid theory of wire fraud called the right-to-control doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Dreeben, I mean, let's say that you win this case because the government presented the right to control as a property interest and now is not even defending that, all right? So I --I just want to -- so let's -- let's -- let's say you win. But -- but you're saying that the government doesn't even have it right now, and I guess I wonder why that's the case. You know, a billion dollars is a lot of property. And, if you take what the government is now saying, you know, frame it as this was an effort to obtain money, the most classic form of property,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, if --if I -- if I understand you correctly, you're saying that in addition -- the government has to prove -- in addition to proving that there was a scheme to obtain property, a scheme to obtain money, the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: We don't have to resolve anything more?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But can't we just --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But you don't -- you don't charge theories."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, you're assuming -- I'm sorry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So you say you object -- that's reserved --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But what -- what if accurate information is the essence of the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't that fraud?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So they certainly were deceived. And the government certainly can try to show that there would be pecuniary loss associated with that, that they paid for services that they didn't get, which is a very conventional type of fraud claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could we decide that the right to control assets isn't a sufficient basis for the prosecution another way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't that false pretenses?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could just start with two main points, one about the scope of property fraud generally and the other about how the right-to-control doctrine fits into that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What about Chiarella? Mr. Dreeben relied on that. How -- how would you say that's different from what is going on here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, I think what's fundamentally different about that and every other case that they cite is, first of all, we think that the findings the jury made in this case, under the right-to-control theory, even without really looking at the rest of the evidence, except for things that are obvious and undisputed, is enough to show that this was actually property fraud."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But -- but you -- you're describing the asset as the actual contract, as the money that was tendered in this transaction, and I didn't understand that to be what the right-to-control theory was about from the Second Circuit's perspective."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And Mr. Dreeben says that's the way you argued the case below. So, suddenly, now we're at this stage with a reinterpretation by the government of what right to control means. And why isn't that a sort of a forfeiture from the standpoint of, if the Court disagrees with you that right to control equals this transaction or even if we don't, haven't you put forward a case that was based on the Second Circuit's conception, and that's how it was argued to the jury, that's how the jury decided it? So why -- why isn't Mr. Dreeben right that if we disagree with that conception of the theory, then we have to reverse?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The core of the right-to-control theory is that a prosecution is allowed to show a deprivation of property simply by showing a deprivation of economically valuable information. You've disavowed that, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you defending the Second Circuit's view that a deprivation of economically valuable information is enough to prove fraud?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the -- the charge here was -- I'm reading directly from the charge -- \"the victim's right to control the use of his assets is injured when it is deprived of potentially valuable economic information that it would consider valuable in deciding how to use his assets.\" Is that an accurate statement of the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "assets -- is \"information that affects the victim's assessment of the benefits or burdens of a\" -- \"of a transaction or relates to the quality of goods or services received or the economic risks of the transaction.\" Is that an accurate statement of the law? This is a jury charge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.87,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What did -- how did it benefit anybody to conceive of the property in the case as the right to control assets rather than to conceive of the property in the case as the contract monies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 0.86,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0002-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I just pick up on Justice Kagan and Justice Jackson's question? Because my understanding is the government's been pushing this theory, and it's not you personally, but the government has been pushing this theory for several decades, and lots of people have been convicted under it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: -- role of the jury? Doesn't the law need to be settled before it goes to the jury so that the jury then makes a determination of whether or not the person is guilty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2ca783a60a6f7f1e990c4942576f41212b2e612835d4218917a5b8163f7a0c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2ca783a60a6f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1170",
